# delv React usage

Wrap the app once in `DelvProvider` so the client is available via context.

## Queries: prefer the `DelvQuery` wrapper component

Use the `DelvQuery` render-prop component as the default way to run queries. It
keeps data fetching declarative and colocated with the markup that renders it.

```jsx
// ✅ PREFERRED
<DelvQuery query={GET_USERS} variables={{id}}>
    {({loading, data, error}) => {
        if(loading) return <Spinner />
        if(error) return <Error error={error} />
        return <UserList users={data.users} />
    }}
</DelvQuery>
```

Use the `useQuery` hook or `withQuery` HOC only when the wrapper component does
not fit (e.g. you need the query result outside of the render tree, or to
compose several hooks together).

```jsx
// Acceptable fallback
const {loading, data, error} = useQuery({query: GET_USERS, variables: {id}})
```

## Mutations: use the `useMutation` hook

There is no wrapper component for mutations, so use the hook. It returns a
`[mutate, {loading, data, error}]` tuple.

```jsx
const [createUser, {loading}] = useMutation({mutation: CREATE_USER})
```
